WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:05.002
Hello, everyone! I'm Mr. Jake. Welcome to Online A two, Book two.

2
00:00:05.302 --> 00:00:08.874
Hi! I'm Sreypich. Let's learn together!

3
00:00:09.174 --> 00:00:14.822
Unit nineteen: Energy at Home. In this unit, you will explain how to save energy.

4
00:00:15.817 --> 00:00:16.678
Energy.

5
00:00:17.378 --> 00:00:20.423
Energy means power used to make machines and lights work.

6
00:00:20.723 --> 00:00:22.641
We use a lot of energy at home.

7
00:00:23.341 --> 00:00:25.645
Your turn. Say: Energy.

8
00:00:28.345 --> 00:00:29.207
Energy.

9
00:00:30.217 --> 00:00:31.508
Electricity.

10
00:00:32.208 --> 00:00:35.090
Electricity means energy that comes through wires.

11
00:00:35.390 --> 00:00:37.134
Electricity is expensive.

12
00:00:37.834 --> 00:00:40.614
Your turn. Say: Electricity.

13
00:00:43.314 --> 00:00:44.594
Electricity.

14
00:00:45.583 --> 00:00:46.225
Solar.

15
00:00:46.925 --> 00:00:48.576
Solar means from the sun.

16
00:00:48.876 --> 00:00:50.771
We have solar panels on our roof.

17
00:00:51.471 --> 00:00:54.286
Your turn. Say: Solar.

18
00:00:56.986 --> 00:00:57.766
Solar.

19
00:00:58.750 --> 00:00:59.461
Light.

20
00:01:00.161 --> 00:01:02.892
Light means a lamp or bulb that makes a room bright.

21
00:01:03.192 --> 00:01:04.692
Turn off the light, please.

22
00:01:05.392 --> 00:01:08.068
Your turn. Say: Light.

23
00:01:10.768 --> 00:01:11.537
Light.

24
00:01:12.550 --> 00:01:13.296
Fan.

25
00:01:13.996 --> 00:01:16.680
Fan means a machine that moves air to cool you.

26
00:01:16.980 --> 00:01:18.527
The fan is on all day.

27
00:01:19.227 --> 00:01:21.833
Your turn. Say: Fan.

28
00:01:24.533 --> 00:01:25.220
Fan.

29
00:01:26.217 --> 00:01:27.218
Switch off.

30
00:01:27.918 --> 00:01:31.682
Switch off means to stop a machine or light by pressing a switch.

31
00:01:31.982 --> 00:01:34.086
Switch off the TV when you leave.

32
00:01:34.786 --> 00:01:37.647
Your turn. Say: Switch off.

33
00:01:40.347 --> 00:01:41.360
Switch off.

34
00:01:42.350 --> 00:01:43.096
Save.

35
00:01:43.796 --> 00:01:45.876
Save means to use less of something.

36
00:01:46.176 --> 00:01:49.511
We save energy by using LED bulbs.

37
00:01:50.211 --> 00:01:52.283
Your turn. Say: Save.

38
00:01:54.983 --> 00:01:55.752
Save.

39
00:01:56.750 --> 00:01:57.449
Bill.

40
00:01:58.149 --> 00:02:00.741
Bill means a paper that tells you how much to pay.

41
00:02:01.041 --> 00:02:03.319
Our electricity bill is lower now.

42
00:02:04.019 --> 00:02:07.380
Your turn. Say: Bill.

43
00:02:10.080 --> 00:02:10.941
Bill.

44
00:02:11.950 --> 00:02:14.089
Now let's listen to a conversation.

45
00:02:14.389 --> 00:02:17.155
Sreypich, how does your family save energy?

46
00:02:18.450 --> 00:02:21.111
We save energy by switching off the lights.

47
00:02:22.417 --> 00:02:23.627
What about the fan?

48
00:02:24.917 --> 00:02:27.056
We switch it off when we leave the room.

49
00:02:28.350 --> 00:02:29.839
Do you use solar power?

50
00:02:31.150 --> 00:02:35.555
Yes! My uncle has solar panels, so his bill is lower.

51
00:02:36.850 --> 00:02:39.523
Grammar focus: By plus verb-ing.

52
00:02:39.823 --> 00:02:42.124
We save energy by switching off the light.

53
00:02:42.424 --> 00:02:44.911
'By + verb-ing' explains how you do something.

54
00:02:45.917 --> 00:02:49.196
Now read and listen. Small Steps, Big Savings.

55
00:02:49.496 --> 00:02:53.005
We use electricity for lights, fans and the TV.

56
00:02:54.317 --> 00:02:57.431
We can save energy by switching off things we don't use.

57
00:02:58.717 --> 00:03:02.376
We also save energy by opening windows instead of using the fan.

58
00:03:03.683 --> 00:03:05.915
Some homes use solar power from the sun.

59
00:03:07.217 --> 00:03:10.157
Saving energy lowers the bill and helps the planet too!

60
00:03:11.450 --> 00:03:14.079
Quiz time! Choose the correct answer.

61
00:03:14.379 --> 00:03:17.098
We save energy blank switching off the light.

62
00:03:17.398 --> 00:03:20.367
A, by. B, with. C, for.

63
00:03:24.383 --> 00:03:26.244
The answer is A: by.

64
00:03:27.750 --> 00:03:29.866
We save money by blank solar power.

65
00:03:30.166 --> 00:03:33.355
A, using. B, use. C, used.

66
00:03:37.350 --> 00:03:38.955
The answer is A: using.

67
00:03:40.450 --> 00:03:42.972
A paper that tells you how much to pay is a blank.

68
00:03:43.272 --> 00:03:46.206
A, bill. B, fan. C, light.

69
00:03:50.217 --> 00:03:51.949
The answer is A: bill.

70
00:03:53.450 --> 00:03:56.996
Now it's your turn to speak. How can your family save energy?

71
00:04:02.296 --> 00:04:08.673
My family can save energy by switching off the fan and lights when we go out, and by using LED bulbs.

72
00:04:08.973 --> 00:04:11.042
Excellent answer, Sreypich!

73
00:04:12.050 --> 00:04:16.235
Great work today! You learned eight new words and by plus verb-ing.

74
00:04:16.535 --> 00:04:20.731
Today's value is responsibility. Help at home and do your jobs.

75
00:04:21.031 --> 00:04:23.417
See you in Unit twenty. Goodbye!

76
00:04:23.717 --> 00:04:26.114
Thank you, Mr. Jake! Bye, everyone!

